# The Myth of the Twin Rivers

In the beginning, two rivers flowed from the same mountain spring—the River of Giving and the River of Returning. Each was governed by a spirit.

The Spirit of Giving possessed five silver fish each dawn. She could cast any number into the sacred pool between the rivers, where they would triple in abundance. The Spirit of Returning would then decide how many to send back upstream.

For many seasons, the Spirit of Giving cast all five fish, trusting completely. The sacred pool shimmered with fifteen fish, and the Spirit of Returning sent back ten, keeping five. Both spirits prospered, their rivers teeming with life.

