The next dawn, the Spirit of Giving received her five fish but withheld them all, trust broken. The sacred pool remained empty. The Spirit of Returning, having consumed her abundance, now had nothing. Both rivers began to dry.

Only when the Spirit of Returning offered repair—returning the trust—did the waters flow again.

The myth reminds us: abundance multiplies through trust, but withholding starves both giver and receiver.
